WEBVTT

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:03.230
<b>Student Council</b>

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:06.050
We're going to do it again this year.

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:08.230
So we need someone to 
host the award ceremony.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.360
You can do it.

00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:13.080
Me?

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:14.360
Akane Sakurai-san.

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:17.780
I'm always listening to your lunch broadcasts.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:22.120
I think you'd be able to make 
it a fun event for everyone.

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:25.090
Okay, got it!

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:26.000
I'll do my best!

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.040
It's happening again this year.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.510
<b>The 15th Annual 
Miss Seiou Contest!!</b>

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:36.260
The contest to decide the school's beauty queen...

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:40.220
The Miss Seiou Contest!

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:43.730
Who's going be crowned this year?

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:21.860
<b>Princess & Pride</b>

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:18.980
Let's see...

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:21.640
Every student has the right to vote,

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:23.520
and everyone may vote one time.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:27.150
The votes will be counted two days 
before the announcement, after school.

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:28.750
Is that right, Vice President?

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:30.880
That's correct.

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:33.590
It's okay for us to vote as well, right?

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:34.750
Of course.

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:37.510
This is kind of exciting.

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:39.630
<b>Broadcast Room</b>

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:39.630
That's pretty cool, Akane-chan!

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:43.560
The student council had you in mind 
specifically to host the ceremony!

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:45.880
Yeah. I need to do a good job.

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:48.520
All right, just leave the sound work to me!

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:49.390
Thanks.

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:52.860
I'm going to go interview some people.

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:53.870
Interview?

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:57.320
I was thinking of putting together a 
special for the lunch broadcast today.

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:02.320
So I'm going to interview some of 
the girls who are favorites to win.

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:04.760
That makes sense!

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:06.890
I was also thinking it'd be good if,

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:09.620
when I host the ceremony, 
I could have the winners

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:13.030
share their personal stories or 
impressions from the contest.

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:14.880
Clever as always, Akane-san!

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:16.960
I'll come help you with your interviews.

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:18.710
Sure.

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:25.600
I think it's great that our school 
lets girls vote for the contest, too.

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:30.730
I wonder who everyone will cast for.

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:32.650
You mean "vote for."

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:34.360
Excuse us.

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:36.600
Good timing.

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:38.450
I'm glad you three are here.

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:41.110
Would you mind if I interviewed you all?

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:43.290
For what?

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:45.120
For the Miss Seiou Contest.

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:48.160
I'd like to make a special program,

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:52.370
so I came to talk to you three, 
as some of the favorites to win.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:57.080
I can't believe I'm a favorite!

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:00.510
I just trying to be thimble.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:01.680
Thimble?

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:04.120
I think she means "humble."

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:06.010
What?

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:08.180
An interview?

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:11.550
Could I get a comment from 
you about the contest?

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:13.840
Well...

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:16.780
I hope everyone has fun.

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:18.980
Like they did at our performance.

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:22.190
You guys were really cool up 
on stage at the culture festival.

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:24.610
Oh, you were listening?

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:27.280
Yeah. Your costumes were great, too.

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:29.200
Thank you!

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:32.410
Well...

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:34.490
If it were a speed sewing contest,

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:37.000
then I'm positive I could win, but...

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:41.960
It'd be nice to have a 
contest like that next time.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:43.520
Yeah.

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:45.890
But you're not just fast.

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:49.260
The stuffed animals you make 
are really cute, Yuuki-san.

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:51.520
Really?

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:54.940
I'll give you one as a present 
next time, Sakurai-senpai.

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:56.730
Thank you!

00:04:56.730 --> 00:05:01.480
It must be hard for the arts and crafts club 
to make all of the dresses for the winners.

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:04.660
But I love making them.

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:05.950
It'll be fun.

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:09.180
Huh? A favorite to win?

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:10.240
I am?

00:05:10.630 --> 00:05:11.710
Of course!

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:13.760
You're the star of the 
rhythmic gymnastics team.

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:14.920
Not at all.

00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:17.540
There are a lot of girls better than me.

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:18.650
For example?

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:23.170
Momoko Sasahara-san?

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:26.880
Sasahara-san's a third-year 
in the ceramics club, right?

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:29.840
She's such an amazing person.

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:34.240
She's kind, and has a soft, clean image, 
like the wild flowers she's named after.

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:36.890
She might not be that great at cooking,

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:39.530
and she panics easily,

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:41.980
but that makes her even cuter.

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:46.100
It's rare to hear you speak so frankly!

00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:48.130
You really admire her, huh?

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:49.870
I guess so...

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:54.580
I'm sure there are plenty of 
girls who'd love to be you, too.

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:56.460
Huh?

00:05:56.860 --> 00:06:00.090
The Miss Seiou Contest?

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:03.460
Oh, yeah. I saw the posters.

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:06.470
What do you think your strengths are?

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:10.810
I try to be fair and square in everything I do...

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:11.870
I guess.

00:06:12.590 --> 00:06:13.840
That's great.

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:14.520
Huh?

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:15.640
You think so?

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:16.680
Yeah.

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:19.440
That's very fitting for you, Kagami-san, 
since you're in the tennis club.

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:22.860
Oh, I see the girls from the broadcast 
committee are doing interviews.

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:26.030
Kagurazaka-senpai!

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:27.960
Good timing.

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:31.480
Kagurazaka-senpai, you're a favorite, too.

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:33.160
Could you give us a comment?

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:35.790
I should be saying the same.

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:38.290
You're quite a favorite yourself.

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:39.310
Huh?

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:41.810
That's not true.

00:06:41.810 --> 00:06:43.920
Besides, I'm going to be the host.

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:49.970
Well, I'm going to go
 interview some other people,

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:51.480
so please excuse me.

00:06:51.480 --> 00:06:53.140
Excuse us.

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:54.640
<b>Broadcast Room</b>

00:06:55.150 --> 00:06:57.770
We need to make it a flashy and fun event.

00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:00.300
You can do it, Akane-chan.

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:01.870
Thank you, Tomo-chan.

00:07:01.870 --> 00:07:07.280
Everyone seemed enthusiastic when 
we took their comments, right?

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:10.220
I think it's because you were there.

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:14.740
You have the ability to draw 
out the good in everyone.

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:19.980
I hope so.

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:21.870
Thank you, Tomo-chan.

00:07:25.140 --> 00:07:28.840
Thank you for coming here, everyone.

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:35.680
We will now begin this year's 
Miss Seiou Contest award ceremony.

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:37.100
Clap, clap, clap.

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:39.440
Oh, Himejima-san.

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:41.560
You're sure working hard.

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:43.350
Shinonome-san and the gang.

00:07:44.370 --> 00:07:45.920
You're about to have lunch?

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:48.640
No, we ate already.

00:07:48.640 --> 00:07:51.050
We're about to have our forest tea party.

00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:52.610
Forest tea party?

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:57.480
<b>Mushroom Forest</b>

00:07:53.150 --> 00:07:57.490
We have Mushroom Forest 
chocolates while we drink tea!

00:07:57.740 --> 00:08:00.000
It's more a gathering of 
people who aren't in clubs.

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:02.920
We all go home after school,

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:08.790
so she said we should get together 
 at lunch, for some reason.

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:13.970
It's such a pain. Why do we have to do this?

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:17.950
A pain? Apologize to the Mushroom Forest!

00:08:17.950 --> 00:08:19.560
Huh?! What are you saying?

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:22.700
I don't really get what's going on,

00:08:22.700 --> 00:08:24.370
but it sounds fun.

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:26.720
But I wouldn't want to get in their way,

00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:27.940
so let's practice elsewhere.

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:32.100
You can go ahead and 
practice here if you want.

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:34.080
Don't mind us.

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:37.680
We'll just be eating snacks, 
drinking tea, and goofing around.

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:40.110
Seriously, why are we doing this?

00:08:40.110 --> 00:08:41.670
They're not just your average snacks!

00:08:41.670 --> 00:08:43.400
They're Mushroom Forest-sama!

00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:45.290
Why add "sama" to them?

00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:51.550
Then, if you have any advice for what 
we could do better, can you let us know?

00:08:52.910 --> 00:08:54.010
You want us to?

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:57.590
Okay, I'll keep going.

00:08:57.890 --> 00:09:00.480
Here, while we're at it. Eat, eat.

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:01.390
Thank you!

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:03.110
Oh, yeah.

00:09:03.110 --> 00:09:05.270
I'll get some drinks in return.

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:08.720
We always have some ready in the broadcast room.

00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:10.620
Hang on a second.

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:14.990
<i>This is an announcement for all students.</i>

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:21.160
<i>The deadline for voting in the 
Miss Seiou Contest is 4 P.M. today.</i>

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:20.020
Miss Seiou Contest
<b>Ballot Box</b>

00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:20.020
There.

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:25.750
<i>Those who haven't voted yet, 
we ask you to please vote now.</i>

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:27.120
<b>Student Council</b>

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:28.630
Miss Seiou Contest
<b>Ballot Box</b>

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:30.780
Time to count the votes.

00:09:30.780 --> 00:09:31.250
Right.

00:09:33.580 --> 00:09:35.010
I'll leave it to you.

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:41.070
I wonder if they're done counting the votes yet.

00:09:41.070 --> 00:09:42.310
Maybe.

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:44.990
I guess we should be heading home.

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:46.440
Yes?

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:48.600
Sakurai-san.

00:09:48.840 --> 00:09:50.640
Oh, Shinomiya-san.

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:51.880
Good work.

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:54.080
I have something to talk to you about.

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:55.010
What is it?

00:09:55.010 --> 00:09:57.240
I have to apologize,

00:09:58.210 --> 00:09:59.490
but could you step down as host?

00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:00.570
What?

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:01.870
Why now?

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:03.790
Actually...

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:07.060
Sakurai-san has been chosen 
as one of the winners.

00:10:07.060 --> 00:10:08.840
I won?

00:10:08.840 --> 00:10:12.290
So I'd like to have someone else be the host...

00:10:12.860 --> 00:10:14.670
Someone else...

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:17.170
Oshii-san, could you do it?

00:10:18.290 --> 00:10:19.200
No way!

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:21.330
I couldn't do it. I couldn't!

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:23.310
Someone from the student 
council should do it.

00:10:23.710 --> 00:10:29.360
We have to attend to the winners backstage 
and keep things running, so we can't.

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:30.810
You really can't?

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:34.090
Why don't you do it, Tomo-chan?

00:10:34.090 --> 00:10:35.490
I couldn't...

00:10:35.490 --> 00:10:37.790
There's no way!

00:10:37.790 --> 00:10:39.220
Okay, Oshii-san.

00:10:39.680 --> 00:10:41.370
You're the host.

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:44.030
What?!

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:46.540
What should I do?

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:50.160
I can't host a huge event like this.

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:51.770
We already have the script.

00:10:51.770 --> 00:10:53.540
You just need the courage to do it.

00:10:53.830 --> 00:10:56.960
I'm better at working behind the scenes.

00:10:56.960 --> 00:10:58.420
I like it more, too.

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:03.290
I've never done anything but simple 
lunchtime announcements, either.

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:04.910
It'll be fine.

00:11:04.910 --> 00:11:05.800
Huh?

00:11:05.800 --> 00:11:08.310
It's not that simple!

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:10.880
You really don't want to?

00:11:10.880 --> 00:11:11.590
Huh?

00:11:11.590 --> 00:11:14.960
I'll decline my win, then.

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:17.570
That way, I can still be the host.

00:11:21.340 --> 00:11:22.520
I'm sorry.

00:11:22.520 --> 00:11:24.830
I was only thinking of myself.

00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:28.950
I didn't even congratulate you.

00:11:29.840 --> 00:11:34.210
It's pretty amazing to place in 
the Miss Seiou Contest, too.

00:11:34.770 --> 00:11:35.970
It's fine.

00:11:35.970 --> 00:11:40.240
I have you do all the school broadcasts, too.

00:11:41.420 --> 00:11:42.640
You know,

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:46.600
I was actually thinking you 
should do the announcements

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:49.470
and host the lunch broadcasts more often.

00:11:49.990 --> 00:11:53.980
I mean, hearing your voice cheers me up.

00:11:57.570 --> 00:11:58.550
Okay!

00:11:59.510 --> 00:12:02.410
I'll try it! I'll try hosting!

00:12:04.430 --> 00:12:06.850
Girl Friend BETA.

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:15.550
I made this fried egg.

00:12:15.550 --> 00:12:17.000
Would you like to try one?

00:12:17.320 --> 00:12:20.340
Oui! I'll have one!

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:21.070
Here.

00:12:21.070 --> 00:12:23.660
<i>Um, what was I supposed to say?</i>

00:12:23.660 --> 00:12:26.070
<i>Akane-chan, what was I supposed to say?</i>

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:27.070
<i>Tomo-chan, the mic's on.</i>

00:12:27.070 --> 00:12:28.230
<i>Huh? Oh, I got it.</i>

00:12:28.230 --> 00:12:29.910
<i>H-Hello, everyone!</i>

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:31.660
<i>Ouch. That hurt.</i>

00:12:31.660 --> 00:12:33.100
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:36.350
<i>It's time for the lunch broadcast!</i>

00:12:36.680 --> 00:12:41.740
<i>And I, Tomo Oshii, will be your ha... your host...</i>

00:12:42.090 --> 00:12:43.360
<i>I messed up.</i>

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:45.200
<i>Calm down, Tomo-chan.</i>

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:47.160
<i>Uh, when this happens...</i>

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:48.800
<i>Oh, yeah! Push buttons!</i>

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:50.120
<i>No, Tomo-chan—</i>

00:12:54.490 --> 00:12:56.410
What was that?

00:12:56.970 --> 00:12:58.130
A crash?

00:12:58.470 --> 00:13:02.880
Come to think of it, I heard Oshii-san 
is going to host the beauty contest.

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:05.100
Not Sakurai?

00:13:05.100 --> 00:13:08.140
According to the rumors, 
Sakurai was selected as a winner.

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:10.760
I wonder if this will be okay.

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:12.020
I don't know.

00:13:12.650 --> 00:13:15.020
I'm sure it'll work out.

00:13:15.720 --> 00:13:19.340
I can't host the ceremony like this.

00:13:19.340 --> 00:13:20.770
That's not true.

00:13:21.080 --> 00:13:22.330
Let's practice.

00:13:22.330 --> 00:13:23.150
Practice.

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:25.210
Practice?

00:13:25.210 --> 00:13:27.160
The event is tomorrow!

00:13:27.590 --> 00:13:31.410
It'll be fine if we practice hard after school.

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:37.420
Th-Thank you for coming here, everyone.

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:45.420
W-We will now begin this year's 
Miss Seiou Contest award ceremony.

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:47.930
Like this?

00:13:48.310 --> 00:13:50.370
Yeah. You're good.

00:13:50.370 --> 00:13:52.280
Good work.

00:13:53.150 --> 00:13:55.000
I see you're practicing hard.

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:55.560
Huh?

00:13:55.940 --> 00:13:58.500
School's out, but you're still here? 
Another gathering?

00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:00.430
No, today's different.

00:14:00.430 --> 00:14:03.260
We wanted to cheer on Oshii-san.

00:14:03.260 --> 00:14:03.690
Huh?

00:14:04.140 --> 00:14:06.330
You're going to host the beauty contest, right?

00:14:06.330 --> 00:14:09.450
We heard you'd be practicing after school.

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:14.140
You brought us drinks last time, too.

00:14:14.140 --> 00:14:16.060
We wanted to thank you.

00:14:17.050 --> 00:14:20.920
Now, think of these mushrooms as your audience!

00:14:21.320 --> 00:14:24.510
Aren't you supposed to imagine 
them as pumpkins, or something?

00:14:24.510 --> 00:14:27.670
Thank you for staying after school just for me.

00:14:28.480 --> 00:14:31.180
If I'm doing anything wrong, let me know.

00:14:31.810 --> 00:14:34.550
I think you should take a better posture.

00:14:34.550 --> 00:14:35.680
R-Right.

00:14:36.200 --> 00:14:39.690
Th-Thank you for coming here, everyone.

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:41.650
You don't have to rush so much.

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:43.320
You can take your time.

00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:51.720
Thank you for coming here, everyone.

00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:54.260
That sounds good.

00:14:52.880 --> 00:14:59.580
We will now begin this year's 
Miss Seiou Contest award ceremony.

00:15:02.230 --> 00:15:04.980
I hope it goes well tomorrow.

00:15:05.360 --> 00:15:07.340
If you do it the way you 
did today, you'll be fine.

00:15:07.640 --> 00:15:10.590
But I'll be in front of the whole school.

00:15:12.130 --> 00:15:14.100
I'm going to practice more when I get home.

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:21.840
I wonder if there's anything 
we can do tomorrow,

00:15:21.840 --> 00:15:23.620
to help out Oshii-san.

00:15:23.620 --> 00:15:26.690
Well, we did stay late and help her practice.

00:15:26.690 --> 00:15:28.990
We can't have her messing up tomorrow.

00:15:29.420 --> 00:15:32.490
Yeah. Maybe we should give 
her some Mushroom Forest.

00:15:33.060 --> 00:15:35.370
Or a costume of that button 
Oshii-san loves so much.

00:15:35.640 --> 00:15:37.240
What kind of costume is that?

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:41.120
I've got a good idea.

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:42.710
Huh?

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:46.460
Seiou Academy Beauty Contest 
<b>Winners' Green Room</b>

00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:49.710
I would like to congratulate 
all of this year's winners.

00:15:50.160 --> 00:15:51.920
Congratulations.

00:15:51.920 --> 00:15:55.350
Please wait here until the ceremony starts.

00:15:55.840 --> 00:15:58.520
Please stand by for now.

00:16:00.360 --> 00:16:01.400
Shiina-san.

00:16:01.400 --> 00:16:03.300
You were picked after all!

00:16:03.300 --> 00:16:05.690
Congratulations to you, too, Sakurai-san.

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:08.940
It's reassuring that we're here together.

00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:12.010
This is a bit too long,

00:16:12.010 --> 00:16:13.400
so I'll make it shorter.

00:16:13.400 --> 00:16:14.680
Thank you.

00:16:14.680 --> 00:16:18.400
You and the others made this dress, right?

00:16:18.400 --> 00:16:19.380
Yeah.

00:16:19.380 --> 00:16:21.540
It's beautiful.

00:16:21.970 --> 00:16:22.960
Really?

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:24.560
Thank you!

00:16:24.560 --> 00:16:26.670
Momoko-chan, did you come up with a speech?

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:29.170
No, not at all.

00:16:29.540 --> 00:16:31.920
Momoko-chan, Nae-chan, over here.

00:16:32.210 --> 00:16:32.850
Huh?

00:16:32.850 --> 00:16:35.140
Smile, please.

00:16:36.550 --> 00:16:38.760
You two second-years over 
there. Let me get a shot.

00:16:42.040 --> 00:16:43.140
Sakurai-san.

00:16:43.140 --> 00:16:45.930
These costumes are so pretty.

00:16:43.650 --> 00:16:45.920
Oh, Kagurazaka-senpai.

00:16:46.310 --> 00:16:48.110
Congratulations.

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:50.250
So you were selected, as well.

00:16:50.250 --> 00:16:53.610
According to the school 
newspaper, it was a sure thing.

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:56.260
Huh? Really?

00:16:56.260 --> 00:17:00.370
I didn't even think I'd get selected.

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:05.870
Well, just how unaware you are is 
one of the nice things about you.

00:17:06.240 --> 00:17:07.500
Sakurai-san.

00:17:08.980 --> 00:17:10.360
Murakami-senpai...

00:17:10.360 --> 00:17:11.790
And Chloe-senpai.

00:17:11.790 --> 00:17:12.880
Congratulations.

00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:15.690
Thank you.

00:17:15.690 --> 00:17:18.880
I like saying "thank you."

00:17:18.880 --> 00:17:22.190
I don't know who voted for me,

00:17:22.610 --> 00:17:24.320
but I'm thankful.

00:17:24.800 --> 00:17:27.230
I'm worried about my speech, though.

00:17:27.590 --> 00:17:29.810
Why don't you say what you said just now?

00:17:30.640 --> 00:17:32.080
I guess you're right.

00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:35.070
And you could add, "I'll be waiting 
at the library," or something.

00:17:35.440 --> 00:17:37.250
That's a good idea.

00:17:37.250 --> 00:17:40.580
More students might come to borrow books then.

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:44.450
As expected, you're a pro at speaking, Akane-san.

00:17:51.520 --> 00:17:53.970
You all look so lovely.

00:17:53.970 --> 00:17:57.800
I'd like to have dinner with all of you someday.

00:17:58.150 --> 00:18:00.420
That sounds great!

00:18:00.420 --> 00:18:03.720
When we do, let me take pictures of each of you!

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:05.890
Dinner and a photoshoot, huh?

00:18:06.660 --> 00:18:09.360
Only ten minutes until the ceremony starts.

00:18:09.730 --> 00:18:11.860
Are all of you ready?

00:18:12.190 --> 00:18:13.090
Yeah.

00:18:13.090 --> 00:18:14.300
We're ready, too.

00:18:14.300 --> 00:18:15.690
All good!

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:17.620
Th-There's trouble!

00:18:17.620 --> 00:18:19.320
Is something the matter?

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:20.870
Sakurai-senpai,

00:18:21.380 --> 00:18:23.240
we can't find Oshii-senpai.

00:18:27.010 --> 00:18:28.400
Tomo-chan!

00:18:27.800 --> 00:18:29.050
Oshii-senpai!

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:29.580
Oshii-san!

00:18:33.860 --> 00:18:38.580
I told her to meet us at the gym 
30 minutes before start time.

00:18:38.580 --> 00:18:40.720
Did she get scared and bail out?

00:18:41.080 --> 00:18:42.900
Tomo-chan wouldn't...

00:18:44.120 --> 00:18:45.600
Maybe she's...

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:54.720
Is everyone excited?!

00:18:54.720 --> 00:18:58.780
Okay. It's time to announce this year's winners!

00:18:59.120 --> 00:18:59.780
Yeah!

00:19:01.510 --> 00:19:03.470
Oh, Akane-chan.

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:06.600
You look so pretty!

00:19:06.600 --> 00:19:08.280
Thank you.

00:19:08.280 --> 00:19:09.790
So you've been practicing all this time.

00:19:10.160 --> 00:19:10.920
Yeah.

00:19:11.280 --> 00:19:15.800
I thought, as long as I'm doing this, 
I should put my own energy into it.

00:19:17.540 --> 00:19:18.550
I'm glad.

00:19:18.890 --> 00:19:19.830
Huh?

00:19:19.830 --> 00:19:22.700
I felt like I'd forced you out into the limelight,

00:19:22.700 --> 00:19:26.410
so I was worried that I'd stressed you out.

00:19:26.800 --> 00:19:30.060
You said you liked working behind the scenes, too.

00:19:30.930 --> 00:19:35.440
But you were making the hosting your own.

00:19:36.120 --> 00:19:37.070
That's great.

00:19:37.720 --> 00:19:40.020
That's not it.

00:19:40.020 --> 00:19:43.160
Everyone helped me practice.

00:19:43.160 --> 00:19:44.570
I knew I had to do my best.

00:19:45.980 --> 00:19:47.020
Plus,

00:19:47.510 --> 00:19:49.430
I'm doing this in your place,

00:19:49.430 --> 00:19:50.830
so I have to do a good job.

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:53.460
Tomo-chan...

00:19:55.090 --> 00:19:57.760
Oh, I have to go.

00:19:57.760 --> 00:19:59.300
The ceremony's going to start.

00:19:59.640 --> 00:20:01.480
Oh, yeah.

00:20:01.480 --> 00:20:02.640
Hang on.

00:20:04.290 --> 00:20:06.640
It's hard to run in that dress, right?

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:13.140
The 15th Annual Miss Seiou Contest

00:20:31.570 --> 00:20:34.070
<b>Mushroom Forest</b>

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:55.720
The 15th Annual Miss Seiou Contest

00:20:46.390 --> 00:20:49.050
The wait is over, everyone!

00:20:49.050 --> 00:20:55.750
We will now begin this year's 
Miss Seiou Contest award ceremony.

00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:56.600
<b>Applause</b>

00:20:57.690 --> 00:20:59.180
<b>Applause   Applause</b>

00:21:09.720 --> 00:21:12.910
I'll be your host today.

00:21:12.910 --> 00:21:15.880
My name is Tomo Oshii, 
from the broadcast committee!

00:21:15.880 --> 00:21:17.460
Thank you, everyone!

00:21:20.220 --> 00:21:23.820
So, it's my first time in such a major role,

00:21:23.820 --> 00:21:26.200
and I'm really nerbus...

00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:27.090
I messed up.

00:21:27.090 --> 00:21:28.090
<b>Laugh</b>

00:21:28.090 --> 00:21:29.420
<b>Laugh       Laugh</b>

00:21:32.940 --> 00:21:36.600
Okay, I'd like this to be a fun ceremony,

00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:39.360
so let's get excited!

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:41.360
<b>Applause</b>

00:21:47.360 --> 00:21:48.850
The 15th Annual Miss Seiou Contest

00:21:47.650 --> 00:21:55.420
That brings an end to this year's 
Miss Seiou Contest award ceremony!

00:21:57.070 --> 00:21:59.750
Did you all have a good time?

00:22:02.360 --> 00:22:05.010
Everyone's really getting into it this year, too.

00:22:05.790 --> 00:22:09.410
That's because Oshii-san 
really worked the crowd.

00:22:09.410 --> 00:22:11.390
It was a good event.

00:22:11.890 --> 00:22:17.390
Now, let's have one more big round 
of applause for the winners!

00:22:20.620 --> 00:22:23.540
Let's also have a round of applause for our host,

00:22:23.540 --> 00:22:27.040
Tomo Oshii, from the broadcast committee!

00:22:32.160 --> 00:22:34.820
<b>You're the best!</b>

00:24:09.920 --> 00:24:24.760
<b>Preview</b>

00:24:10.630 --> 00:24:11.470
Japan has a saying,

00:24:11.470 --> 00:24:14.080
"Goodbye triangle, come again square,"

00:24:14.080 --> 00:24:15.890
that's similar to "see you later, alligator."

00:24:15.890 --> 00:24:17.970
Why does the triangle get kicked out,

00:24:18.170 --> 00:24:20.620
while the square gets invited back?

00:24:20.620 --> 00:24:24.670
Next time: "Goodbye à la Mode."

00:24:20.680 --> 00:24:24.760
<b>Episode 11: Goodbye à la Mode</b>
